From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 06:05:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp: Implement
 ICompositorInterop::CreateCompositionSurfaceForSwapChain().

A surface of a swapchain made for composition shows what the swapchain
presented last: the texture dxgi keeps of it, drawn as a bitmap on the
target's Direct2D context, or brought over to the target's device
first when that is another one, the way the tiles of drawing surfaces
already were (that copy is now shared by both).  Surface brushes and
nine-grids draw either kind of surface.

As on Windows, what a swapchain presents is shown without a commit: on
each present the targets are drawn again, as they stand, on the
compositor's thread.  The present only queues that, since the
presenting thread may not take the compositor's lock.

Only a swapchain made for composition can be shown; anything else is
E_INVALIDARG.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

